<p>A quotation (proposal) is what you send before the customer confirms: the system, price, subsidy and how much they will save. When they accept, it becomes the invoice in one click.</p>
<h4>Create a quotation</h4>
<ol class="steps">
    <li>From a lead: <span class="btnname">Create quotation for this lead</span>. From a customer: <span class="btnname">Quotation</span>. Or <span class="path">Sales → Quotations</span> → <span class="btnname">New Quotation</span> and pick a customer or lead, or just type the name and phone of a new enquiry.</li>
    <li>Enter the kW. The <strong>kit</strong> for that kW and the <strong>expected subsidy</strong> (PM Surya Ghar: ₹30,000/kW up to 2 kW, ₹18,000 for the 3rd kW, max ₹78,000) are filled in; change them if needed.</li>
    <li>Click <span class="btnname">Fill as B2C package</span> (one system line + installation line) or <span class="btnname">Load items (B2B)</span> (every item), or type the lines.</li>
    <li>Choose who pays the <strong>EB / meter charges</strong>, check <strong>units per kW per day</strong> and the <strong>tariff</strong> (defaults from <span class="path">Settings → Quotation</span>), the terms, and optionally attach a <strong>design / roof layout</strong> image or PDF.</li>
    <li><span class="btnname">Save quotation</span>. It gets a number like <code>QT/2026-27/0001</code>.</li>
</ol>
<h4>What the customer sees</h4>
<p>The PDF has your logo, the lines with GST, total, EB / meter charges, expected subsidy and <strong>net cost</strong>, plus <strong>Your savings</strong>: generation per year, savings per year, <strong>payback in years</strong> and savings over 25 years.</p>
<h4>Send it</h4>
<ul>
    <li><span class="btnname">WhatsApp</span> opens WhatsApp with a message and a private link to the PDF (the customer does not need to log in).</li>
    <li><span class="btnname">Email</span> sends the PDF as an attachment.</li>
    <li>Either marks the quotation <em>Sent</em>. When the customer opens the link, the quotation shows <i class="bi bi-eye text-success"></i> "Customer opened the link" with the time.</li>
</ul>
<h4>Statuses</h4>
<p><span class="badge text-bg-secondary">Draft</span> → <span class="badge text-bg-info">Sent</span> → <span class="badge text-bg-primary">Accepted</span> / <span class="badge text-bg-danger">Rejected</span> → <span class="badge text-bg-success">Converted to invoice</span>. Set them with the buttons on the quotation. Quotations past their "valid until" date show as expired in the list.</p>
<h4>Convert to invoice</h4>
<ol class="steps">
    <li>Click <span class="btnname">Convert to invoice</span>. For a lead or new enquiry, the customer is created first (the lead is marked confirmed).</li>
    <li>The invoice form opens filled from the quotation (lines, kW, kit, subsidy type, meter charges). Choose the payment mode, check and save.</li>
    <li>The quotation is marked <em>Converted</em> and links to the invoice. A converted quotation cannot be edited.</li>
</ol>
<h4>Delete a quotation</h4>
<ul>
    <li>For a wrong or duplicate quotation: open it → <span class="btnname">Delete</span> and confirm. Its lines and 3D layout picture are removed; a 3D design it was made from stays.</li>
    <li>Only roles with <em>Quotations: delete</em> (<span class="path">Administration → Roles &amp; Access</span>) see the button.</li>
    <li>A quotation already converted to an invoice cannot be deleted (cancel or delete the invoice instead).</li>
</ul>
